Package: pam-hkpac
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: PAM module that caches the login password into the user keyring
 pam_hkpac is a small PAM module which, after authentication has succeeded,
 reads the plaintext password from the PAM authentication token (PAM_AUTHTOK)
 set by the authentication module and stores it into the user keyring (@u,
 key name "ACpass"), so that later single sign-on (SSO) consumers can reuse it
 without prompting the user again.
 .
 The module performs no authentication itself and never talks to the PAM
 conversation: it only reads PAM_AUTHTOK and always returns PAM_IGNORE, so it
 cannot interfere with the modules that carry out the real authentication
 (e.g. pam_deepin_authentication.so).
 .
 It is inserted by the package maintainer scripts into /etc/pam.d/lightdm,
 right after the "auth substack common-auth" line.  It must not be placed
 inside common-auth: before pam_deepin_authentication.so it would steal the
 single PAM conversation response of the greeter, and after it the
 [success=end] jump would skip it.
